On 28 Mar 2026, I asked Mike if we could start a new thread, as the old one was so large
it was slowing down the whole computer.  It turned out to be easy by pasting in about 10
lines of information he gave me.  Unfortunately, this loses the context, so I have to
train him again in my python code preferences

    - All triple strings use ''' if possible
    - All conditionals and functions/classes have a newline after the ':'
    - Functions and classes names with CamelCase names
    - Global and local variables lower-case snake case
    - No blank lines at all between code
    - Math formatting for binary operators
        - No space around *, /, //, **
        - Space on each side of +, -, %, &, |, <<, >>, <, <=, >, >=, !=, ==, or, and
    - Use type annotations wherever possible


